## Implementation Details

### Audio And Chapters

- Implement Rust commands:
  - `audio probe --input <path>` returns `{ "duration_ms": number }`.
  - `audio cut --input <path> --output <path> --windows-json <path> --mode fade|exact --fade-ms <n> --encoding vbr|cbr`.
  - `audio bleep --input <path> --output <path> --windows-json <path> --beep-frequency-hz <n> --beep-volume <f> --duck-volume <f> --encoding vbr|cbr`.
  - `audio split --input <path> --out-dir <path> --chunk-size-bytes <n>` returns chunk paths and offsets.
  - `chapters write --audio <path> --chapters-json <path> --removed-windows-json <path>`.
- Keep ffmpeg as the execution engine for probe, split, bleep, cut, and concat. Rust owns window merging, keep-segment planning, ffmpeg argument construction, temp-file handling, and atomic output replacement.
- Preserve current encoding behavior: LLM ad removal uses VBR/fade, chapter strategy uses exact CBR cuts, profanity bleeping keeps existing beep/duck semantics.
- Replace Python calls in `podcast_processor/audio.py` and chapter writing only through wrapper functions, with Python fallback on Rust CLI error.

### Feed XML

- Implement Rust commands:
  - `feed render --db <sqlite> --feed-id <id> --base-url <url> --include-unprocessed true|false --feed-token <id> --feed-secret <secret>`.
  - `feed render-aggregate --db <sqlite> --user-id <id> --base-url <url> --require-auth true|false --limit-per-feed 3 --feed-token <id> --feed-secret <secret>`.
- Rust opens SQLite read-only with `PRAGMA query_only=ON` and the same busy timeout policy as Python.
- Python routes keep auth, feed token validation, writer-side `last_used_at` updates, ETag, Last-Modified, 304 handling, and response headers.
- Rust renders only the XML body and must match current behavior for:
  - feed title, link, image, lastBuildDate, namespaces;
  - post ordering and aggregate limit-per-feed behavior;
  - enclosure URL `/post/<guid>.mp3` plus feed token query params;
  - enclosure length from `processed_audio_path` file size or `0`;
  - CDATA descriptions, `content:encoded`, `itunes:image`, `itunes:duration`;
  - Podly chapter HTML derived from `post.chapter_data`.
- Python falls back to existing PyRSS2Gen rendering if Rust fails.

### Transcript And Word Timestamp Serialization

- Add a writer action `finish_transcription_replace_from_artifact`.
- During transcription, write large word timestamp payloads to a job-scoped artifact file instead of sending the nested list through writer IPC.
- The writer receives only `{ post_id, model_call_id, segment_count, artifact_path }`, validates the artifact path is under the job/instance data root, and invokes:
  - `transcript normalize-word-timestamps --input <path> --output <path>`.
- Rust streams the artifact and writes compact JSON text. The writer stores that JSON text in `post.transcript_word_timestamps` using the writer service, without materializing the nested Python object graph.
- Add `transcript export-word-timestamps --db <sqlite> --post-id <id>` for read-heavy paths that can consume word timestamps from a short-lived Rust process instead of loading large JSON through ORM state.
- Keep the existing `Post.transcript_word_timestamps` column and external behavior unchanged for this phase. No Alembic migration is required.

## Test Plan

- Add Rust unit tests for window merging, keep-segment planning, duration formatting, CDATA escaping, chapter timestamp recalculation, feed token URL appending, and transcript JSON streaming.
- Add Python tests that monkeypatch `podly_tools` success/failure and verify fallback behavior for audio, feed XML, and transcript artifact writes.
- Add feed XML parity tests: seed feeds/posts/chapter data, render with Python and Rust, normalize XML, and assert semantic equivalence.
- Add transcript tests proving large word timestamp payloads go through artifact-path writer action and store the same JSON value currently produced.
- Add audio/chapter parity tests using small fixture audio where practical; otherwise assert generated ffmpeg command plans and wrapper behavior.
- Run only `./scripts/ci.sh` for backend verification after implementation, per project rules.

## Assumptions And Defaults

- Rust sidecar rollout is phased and opt-in at first.
- Rust orchestrates ffmpeg instead of replacing audio codecs.
- Rust may read SQLite directly for feed XML and transcript export, but all writes remain inside the writer service.
- The first phase avoids schema migrations and preserves existing API, RSS, audio, and DB behavior.
- Temporary Rust feature flags should be removed or defaulted on only after parity tests and live memory measurements show stable improvement.
